  "final_message": "If you call `retry.call_with_retry()` without a `max_attempts` argument, it makes at most **4** attempts in total, and that count includes the first try.\n\n- In `retry.py`, a `max_attempts` of `None` falls back to `DEFAULT_MAX_ATTEMPTS = 4`.\n- The loop runs `for _ in range(attempts)`. It returns as soon as a call succeeds; if all 4 calls fail, it re-raises the last exception.\n- `main7.py` calls it with no argument, so it gets this default.\n- The other numbers in the folder don't affect it. `retry.py` never imports `RETRY_LIMIT = 5` (in `decoy_backoff.py`) or `MAX_RETRIES = 3` (in `decoy_network.py`). `.amplifier/settings.local.yaml` has no retry settings.\n\nANSWER: 4",
